---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
	<article class="narrative">
		<h1>
			Hi, I’m <strong>Alejandro Ramírez</strong>, an{" "}
			<strong>Automation &amp; Integrations Engineer</strong> based in Berlin.
		</h1>

		<p>
			I build reliable systems for work that should not need manual coordination:
			accounting posting, supplier-document processing, CRM intake, data reconciliation,
			and internal tools. The work usually starts with a real operational problem—a team
			copying data between systems, checking the same document twice, or trying to recover
			from an automation nobody fully trusts.
		</p>

		<p>
			At Ko Kitchen, I build the systems around those gaps. That includes a fail-closed{" "}
			<a href="/work/sumup-lexware-fail-closed">SumUp → Lexware accounting workflow</a>{" "}
			that blocks uncertain data instead of guessing, a{" "}
			<a href="/work/hamberger-invoices-lexware">supplier-invoice pipeline</a>{" "}that
			creates idempotent Lexware purchase records from PDFs, and a scheduled{" "}
			<a href="/work/payout-evidence-attachments">payout-evidence workflow</a>{" "}that keeps
			source documents with the accounting voucher they support.
		</p>

		<p>
			Before that, I co-founded JurisDATA. A high-ranking SEO article became an automated
			intake and guidance system that helped more than 50,000 people. It connected
			ticket-data retrieval, Airtable, Make, webhook monitoring, and WhatsApp and email
			delivery. The technical challenge was not only scale. It was making a complex system
			useful while keeping personal data, legal rules, and operational details private. The{" "}
			<a href="/work/jurisdata-ticket-intake">public case study</a>{" "}explains the
			architecture.
		</p>

		<p>
			I also build public developer tools.{" "}
			<a href="https://github.com/faramirezs/hamberger-dl">hamberger-dl</a>{" "}is a command-line
			tool for downloading supplier documents with OIDC login, token caching, filters, ZIP
			export, and safe re-runs. In open source, I contributed a Rust streaming LLM-provider
			worker to iii; the work was{" "}
			<a href="https://github.com/iii-hq/workers/pull/690">approved and merged</a>.
		</p>

		<p>
			I work across n8n, Make, Python, APIs, data pipelines, SQL, Docker, and backend
			systems. 42 Berlin strengthened my foundation in C, C++, Unix, networking,
			concurrency, and systems programming.
		</p>

		<p>
			I do my best work on high-friction problems where I can understand the system gap,
			own the integration, and ship a result people can rely on.
		</p>

		<p class="contact">
			Find me on{" "}<a href="https://github.com/faramirezs">GitHub</a>{" "}and{" "}
			<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alejandro-mlops-engineer/">LinkedIn</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	.narrative {
		max-width: 46rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: var(--spacing-4xl) var(--spacing-lg);
		font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-2xl);
		font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-display);
		letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
		line-height: 1.25;
	}

	p {
		margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-xl);
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration-color: var(--color-border);
		text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
		text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--transition-fast);
	}

	a:hover {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	.contact {
		margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
		color: var(--color-muted);
	}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.narrative {
			padding: var(--spacing-3xl) var(--spacing-lg);
			font-size: var(--font-size-base);
		}

		h1 {
			font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
		}
	}
</style>
